Changelog: 10-10-2026 21:23:00

Release tool tests no longer depend on the checksums pinned in portal/apps.toml. They failed once the first releases were pinned, because a local build (another mtime) never matches a real release. test_build_release pins bazzite-test to its own local build (build_release.py reads the manifest from one MANIFEST constant, so a test can point it at a copy) and gains a test that a wrong pin is refused; test_pin_app reads the old tag and checksum from the manifest; tools/installer-tests/release.sh runs on a copy of the checkout where pin_app.py pins bazzite-test and governor to their local builds, so the bundle and the fetched governor release are checked against a real pin. The release tools themselves behave as before.

